# How to cite this software.
#
# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file.
#
# This describes the software, not a paper: there is deliberately no
# 'preferred-citation' here, so the button always offers the software itself.
# Papers to cite alongside it are listed in the README's Citation section.
#
# The author order is deliberate, and 'pyproject.toml' repeats the version
# below, so the two change together.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: "FASTER"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based platform for running, managing, and reviewing federated-learning
  experiments. A single-page dashboard drives a database-backed application layer and
  a bundled Job Manager that queues training jobs, launches workers, and persists
  shared state, so an experiment is configured, submitted, monitored, and exported
  without leaving the browser. Alongside the standard aggregation baselines it ships
  FedGP, an evolutionary aggregation method that searches for the aggregation function
  with genetic programming.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/HISTLab-hevs/FASTER"
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - genetic programming
  - evolutionary computation
  - model aggregation
  - reproducibility

